    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier offensive anchor with a score of 81.88. He benefits from a prime matchup against a pitcher with a 4.75 xERA, compounded by significant positive park and platoon adjustments that elevate his ceiling. **Drake Baldwin** is our next strongest play (71.83); leading off against a struggling starter in a favorable park, his recent form and top-of-the-order security make him a foundational piece. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-focused assets, with **Jackson Merrill** (68.51) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) both posting elite scores. Their ability to exploit favorable matchups against slower deliveries makes them essential in our pursuit of the stolen base category, which remains our primary point of emphasis given its scarcity.\n\nThe bench decision process was tightest regarding **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose 54.41 projection narrowly missed the cut. While he benefits from the same favorable matchup as **Nasim Nunez** and **Curtis Mead**, his projected efficiency dipped due to an unfavorable platoon split and a lower-tier batting order position compared to our starters. Consequently, we opted for the higher upside of **Jackson Merrill** and the positional versatility offered by our core MI/UTIL slots. We are closely monitoring **Heliot Ramos** (65.86); while he faces a tough right-handed arm, the wind blowing out works in his favor, though we remain wary of the opponent's elite catcher defense which slightly penalizes his SB expectation. Overall, we are well-positioned for an efficient day, provided the weather conditions hold and our primary hitters capitalize on the current SP xERA vulnerabilities.",
